module latte_app
kind library

# `latte_app` is the composition root: the one place that names BOTH halves of
# latte and wires them onto espresso.
#
# It is a sibling module rather than a package under `latte/` because a package
# under a module may not import its own module root — `latte.web` cannot name
# `CircuitSet` or `ShellOptions` for exactly that reason, which is why a
# `CircuitSeam` is nine closures over std types. A separate module has no such
# restriction, so the assembling that every application used to hand-write can
# live here instead of in every `main.b`.
#
# Nothing under `latte/`'s module root imports this, so latte's core stays
# free of espresso and its wasm leg is unaffected.
require path ".."
require github.com/beans-lang/espresso v0.3.0
require github.com/beans-lang/barista v0.1.1
